      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The clinical and neuroradiologic findings and surgical results in a series of 19 patients with lateral ventricle meningioma, operated on during a 33-year period, are described. This experience is compared with that of previous workers and the following conclusions are drawn: these tumors have no characteristic symptoms; preoperative diagnosis requires both computed tomography scans and carotid and vertebral angiography; the safest surgical approach is through a sagittal or oblique parietooccipital cortical incision to avoid damage to motor, visual, and speech areas of the cortex."},
